## 2️⃣ LOGIN - Get JWT Token

### Endpoint
```
POST http://localhost:8080/account/login
```

### Headers
```
Content-Type: application/json
```

### Login User 1
```json
{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}
```

### Login User 2
```json
{
  "email": "jane.smith@example.com",
  "password": "securePass456"
}
```

### Login Admin
```json
{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "admin123"
}
```

### Expected Response
```json
{
  "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJqb2huLmRvZUBleGFtcGxlLmNvbSIsImlhdCI6MTcwMDAwMDAwMCwiZXhwIjoxNzAwMDg2NDAwfQ.xxxxx",
  "userId": "507f1f77bcf86cd799439011"
}
```

**💡 Copy the `token` value - you'll need it for protected endpoints!**

